  "body": "Stacked on #1064 (base it on `main` and merge after #1064).\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed, by #1056's points\n\n1. **A stock copy carries its source's reduced-fidelity flag (done).** `SetStock` writes the copied model's chord error onto the `FromModel` stock, and its undo restores the stock's old flag. `UpdateModel`'s propagation trades the flag with the copy's facets both ways. `CreateSetup`'s datum clone and `DeleteSetup`'s undo carry it in `StockSnap`. `DeleteEntity` already restored any entity's flag. The project saves it on the stock row (the existing `coarse_mm` key), and the loader restores it for `FromModel` stocks. Deleting or renaming the source no longer stops the laws tightening. A refusal still names the model the facets came from, even after that model is deleted.\n2. **Older projects (partly done, rest left open).** A stock from a #911-era file, where the flag lived only on the model, takes its source's flag on load (`model_fidelity::adopt_copies`). Files from before #911 are **not** handled. The version did not change with #911, so whether such a file holds a coarse STEP mesh cannot be known. Fixing that is file-format work: a version bump plus a \"fidelity unknown\" mark that is saved with the file, and then a choice between refusing and a named note. That is above this slice. It is recorded in `docs/decisions/1056-fidelity-flag-gaps.md` and left on #1056.\n3. **The named refusal wins (done).** New `model_fidelity::program_tol`: when the gate refuses a program op for its model's fidelity, it returns that refusal as `Err`; otherwise it returns `verdict_tol`. `stock_sim::simulate_document` and `stock_sim_carry::judge` read it. The case found: a fine part in a stock copied from a too-coarse model, after that model is deleted. More generally, any op whose fidelity floor sits under the sim's 0.01 mm. The gate used to print a gouge line next to the refusal; now it prints the refusal alone, and the sim says it did not judge.\n4. **Display tolerances (done).** `FieldView` gains `tol`, the tolerance its colours are gated at, filled from `program_tol` by `field_view` and by playback (`PlaySeed`/`FieldPlay`). `machined_classes::mesh_classes`, `ui` `trace/eye.rs` and `trace/cpu_eye.rs` read it instead of `DEV_TOL`. On a refused program the picture has no target, and its note gives the refusal.\n\n## How tested\n\nNew suite `crates/app/tests/fidelity_copies.rs`:\n- `a_stock_copy_keeps_its_flag_when_its_source_is_deleted`: delete, undo and redo; the refusal by the source's name still stands after the delete; box stocks stay unflagged.\n- `the_copy_follows_its_source_through_updates_and_setup_clones`: UpdateModel and its undo, CreateSetup clone, DeleteSetup and its undo.\n- `the_copys_flag_rides_the_project_file_and_an_older_copy_adopts_its_source`: the key is on the stock row, the file round-trips byte for byte, and a file with the key removed takes the source's flag on load.\n- `the_named_refusal_wins_over_a_gouge_line_the_sim_would_read`: checked to fail without the fix. The gate printed `gouge: program cuts below the model in 2048 cell(s)` next to the refusal.\n- `the_eyes_colours_are_gated_at_the_tightened_verdict_tolerance`: `field_view` and `FieldPlay::view` give 0.01 - excess on a 0.012 mm model, and `DEV_TOL` at full fidelity.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/904-reduced-fidelity-laws` is green on the final head (app suites and ui suites). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The GPU and CPU eyes' changed argument (`fv.tol`) is covered only by the build and by the ui `trace_composite`/`trace_parity` suites at `DEV_TOL`. No pixel or snapshot run was done; snapshots are in the release lane.\n- Projects saved before #911 (point 2, above).\n\nNo goldens or snapshot PNGs changed. `docs/decisions/1056-fidelity-flag-gaps.md` records the choices.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nChangelog: A stock copied from a coarse STEP model keeps its reduced-fidelity flag after the model is deleted, and the project file saves it. A fidelity refusal is no longer joined by a gouge line from the sim. The stock view's colours use the tightened tolerance (#1056).\n\nRefs #1056\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
